  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "Evidence: The two completed experiments (config_010, config_020) both use scgpt + multiprofile + avgpool + weighted, differing only in image encoder. config_020 (imagenet_vit_l) achieves the best accuracy (0.542) at a lower cost (2.94 GPU hrs) than config_010 (resnet50, 0.525, 4.42 GPU hrs). The remaining uncertainty is whether the simple avgpool aggregation is bottlenecking performance—averaging multiple profiles discards inter-profile structure that a transformer could capture. This experiment (config_019: scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) isolates the aggregation change while keeping the best-performing base (scgpt + vit_l + weighted fusion), making the result interpretable. It is the best use of experiment 3 because it tests the single most impactful architectural lever (aggregation) on the current best configuration, and a positive result would justify further exploitation of the transformer+vit_l direction in remaining budget. Expected relative cost: transformer aggregation adds attention computation over multiple profiles, so I estimate ~3.5–4.5 GPU hrs—moderately more expensive than config_020's 2.94 hrs but still within a reasonable range, and justified by the potential accuracy gain."
}

